==Format==
The 1982 tournament introduced the expanded 36-team format, a significant increase from the 24 teams used in the 1978 edition. The format consisted of three phases:

# '''First group stage''': 36 teams divided into six groups of six. Each group played a round-robin, with the top two teams from each group advancing to the second group stage. Three points were awarded for a win, one for a draw, and none for a loss.
# '''Second group stage''': 12 teams divided into four groups of three. Each group played a round-robin, with the group winner advancing to the semi-finals.
# '''Knockout stage''': The four semi-finalists competed in single-elimination matches, with extra time and a penalty shootout (if necessary) used to decide the winner. The semi-final winners advanced to the final, while the losers contested the third-place match.

The two-group-stage format was controversial among some pundits, who argued that it produced too many matches and rewarded defensive play in the second group stage. However, it also allowed for greater representation from emerging football nations and produced several memorable matches. The format would be used again in 1986 before being replaced by a single group stage with a preliminary knockout round.

