Group A was dominated by hosts Okaiken and Volisania, who both finished on 10 points. Okaiken topped the group on goal difference after a decisive 3–0 victory over Laga in the final round of matches. Galwa finished third on 8 points, a strong showing that ultimately was not enough to advance. The group's most memorable match was Okaiken's 2–1 victory over Volisania on the opening day, played before 79,871 fans at Tenji Park Olympic Stadium—the largest crowd in AFA World Cup history at the time.

