Group F was the most competitive group, with four teams still in contention for the two qualifying spots on the final day. Breisland's defensive discipline—conceding only three goals in five matches—proved the foundation of their group-winning campaign. Varkana secured second place with a 2–0 victory over Pasundan, while Nusaraya's 1–1 draw with Balboa eliminated both teams.

