Group 4 was the most dramatic of the second-round groups. Hosts Okaiken opened with a 1–1 draw against Burawa, setting up a decisive final match against Volisania. In front of 72,000 fans at Toyozawa National Stadium, Okaiken prevailed 2–1 with goals in each half, the winner coming from a set piece in the 73rd minute. The victory sent the host nation into the semi-finals and sparked celebrations across Okaiken.

==Knockout stage==
The knockout stage consisted of two semi-finals, a third-place match, and the final. All matches were played in Okaiken.

===Semi-finals===

