Balisca ended the host nation's dream of a World Cup final on home soil with a 2–1 victory at Tenji Park Olympic Stadium. [[Matías Varela]] opened the scoring in the 34th minute, rising above the Okaiken defense to head home a [[Diego Ramírez]] cross. Okaiken equalized in the 56th minute through [[Kenji Hattori]], who drove a low shot from 20 meters after a flowing counter-attack. The match seemed destined for extra time until Ramírez struck in the 78th minute, curling a free kick from the edge of the area past the Okaiken wall. The goal silenced the 79,871-strong crowd and sent Balisca to the final.

====Semi-final 2: Asikyira vs Sanrobonia====

{{football box
