Sanrobonia claimed third place with a 2–0 victory over a deflated Okaiken side still reeling from their semi-final defeat. [[Ricardo Fuentes]] opened the scoring in the 23rd minute with a composed finish after a swift counter-attack, and [[Miguel Torres]] sealed the result in the 81st minute with a long-range strike that curled past the Okaiken goalkeeper. The loss meant Okaiken finished fourth—their best World Cup result to date, but a bitter disappointment for a nation that had dreamed of a home final.

