Balisca defeated Asikyira 3–1 in the final to claim their second AFA World Cup title. The match was played before a capacity crowd of 79,871 at Tenji Park Olympic Stadium, with an estimated global television audience of 1.2 billion viewers.

[[Matías Varela]] opened the scoring in the 31st minute with a powerful header from a [[Diego Ramírez]] cross. Asikyira equalized in the 55th minute through [[Youssef Al-Hassan]], who rose highest to meet a corner kick and power a header past [[Carlos Mendes]]. The Baliscan response was immediate—Ramírez restored the lead just four minutes later, cutting inside from the right wing and driving a low shot into the far corner. Varela sealed the victory with his eighth goal of the tournament in the 76th minute, finishing a counter-attack that began in Balisca's own penalty area.

The victory marked Balisca's second AFA World Cup title and cemented Varela's status as one of world football's emerging stars.

